\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Decoding and test-time compute belong to evaluation}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{We formulate the model and evaluation protocol as separate inputs because
one next-token law supports many procedures. Greedy decoding, temperature
sampling, majority voting, verifier-guided selection, and multi-round tool use
can produce different outcome laws from the same checkpoint. The sampling and
selection procedures in \citet{secs. 3--4}{shao2024deepseekmath} are concrete
examples.}

\p{Accordingly, a comparison that changes #{b_{\mathrm{eval}}} or
#{\mathsf I} does not estimate a training-only effect. Later potential
frontiers retain evaluation-time compute as a coordinate rather than hiding it
inside a model score.}
